#11028
The mouth of the bay~
   Before you is the vast and terrible ocean.  As your boat slips over the 
gurgling waves, they seem to cackle in contempt.  Though the ocean may challenge
you, may claim your puny life at any whim, you will never challenge the ocean.
It stands before you like a thousand Leviathans, deep and bitter.  You shudder
as you hear them howl with delight as they crash their mighty waves against
the dangerous crags to the south.
~
