waves, plummeting down, eardrums throbbing fearful of a coming wreck.  In fair
wind or foul, the sea is a raging storm.  Your heart yearns for some companion
to chaperone you over these bitter fathoms.  To the west, a large bay cuts
into the black basalt cliffs.  You can see a small volcano rising from the
sea to the east.
~
