#11110
The small volcano.~
A rugged slope of sharp igneous and metamorphic rock (pumice, obsidian
granite and basalt) extruded from the sea.  The harsh terrain slopes up
from the sea, then down into a small caldera.  You can feel the heat of 
the lava even here through the soles of your boots.  A thoroughly unpleasant
and unsafe place to visit.
~
