#11203
By the River Lethe.~
    A sepulcher floats upon the river Lethe running through this deep and
unholy cavity.  It reflects the filth of all humanity, a nightmare crammed with
unfathomable things:  witches roasting foetuses in a pan, crones at a mirror
served by naked girls who straighten stockings to entice a Fiend.  
Yet one beast stands out, uglier and fouler than the rest, and this is Boredom,
dreaming of hangings while he puffs his pipe -- I think you know him well, 
reader, my twin!
~
